  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0165 database is designed to store information about athletes, coaches, events, and other related data. The athlete table contains detailed information about each athlete, including their code, name, function, country, height, weight, birth date, and other personal details. The coach table stores information about coaches, including their code, name, function, category, country, and disciplines they specialize in. The event table contains information about each event, including its name, tag, sport, and sport code. The medalist table stores information about medal winners, including the date they won the medal, the type of medal, their name, country, and event details. The medal table contains a summary of medals won by each country, including the type of medal, code, date, and event details. The medal_total table stores the total number of gold, silver, and bronze medals won by each country. The schedule table contains information about the schedule of events, including the start and end dates, status, discipline, and event details. The schedule_preliminary table stores preliminary information about the schedule, including the estimated start time, venue, and event details. The team table stores information about each team, including their code, name, country, discipline, and athletes and coaches associated with them. The torch_route table stores information about the torch relay route, including the title, city, start and end dates, and tag. The venue table contains information about each venue, including its name, sports, and start and end dates.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project focuses on developing a comprehensive data analytics and data warehouse solution for the Paris 2024 Olympic Summer Games. The system will manage and analyze data related to the event, encompassing participating countries, athletes, sports disciplines, medal standings, event details, and more. This repository provides a structured framework for processing and understanding extensive datasets associated with the 2024 Olympics.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To create an efficient data warehouse for storing and managing data related to the Paris 2024 Olympics.\n- To provide tools and functionalities for analyzing various aspects of the Olympic data, such as athlete performance, medal standings, and event schedules.\n- To support data-driven decision-making and insights generation for stakeholders involved in the Olympics.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Olympic Organizing Committee: Oversees the setup and operation of the Olympics, using data for planning and logistics.\n- Athletes and Coaches: Access performance data and schedules for strategic preparation and participation.\n- Sports Analysts and Journalists: Utilize data insights for reporting and analysis of the event.\n- Fans and Spectators: Access event schedules and results.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Athlete Management: Manage data related to athletes, including personal information, disciplines, and event participation.\n- Coach Management: Store and manage coach details and their roles within different sports disciplines.\n- Event Schedule and Results: Manage event scheduling, phases, and results tracking, including medal distribution.\n- Medal Tracking: Record and analyze medal standings by country and event.\n- Team Management: Manage data related to teams, including athletes and coaches details.\n- Venue and Torch Route Management: Track venues and torch relay routes with related details and scheduling.\n  \n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The system should efficiently handle large volumes of data related to multiple aspects of the Olympic Games.\n- Performance: Ensure quick data retrieval and analysis capabilities.\n- Security: Implement robust security measures to protect sensitive data, including personal information of athletes and event details.\n- Usability: Provide user-friendly interfaces for different stakeholders to interact with the data system seamlessly.\n- Reliability: Ensure data accuracy and system uptime during the Olympic Games period for real-time access.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0165.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0165\nCREATE TABLE `athlete` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `function` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `height` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `weight` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birth_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `coach` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `function` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `disciplines` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `event` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tag` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `sport` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `sport_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medalist` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `date_won` date NOT NULL,\n  `medal_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `event_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `medalist_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`event_id`) REFERENCES `event` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medal` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `medal_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `event_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `medal_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`event_id`) REFERENCES `event` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medal_total` (\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `gold` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `silver` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `bronze` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `schedule` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `discipline` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `event_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `schedule_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`event_id`) REFERENCES `event` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `schedule_preliminary` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `estimated_start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `venue` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `event_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `schedule_preliminary_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`event_id`) REFERENCES `event` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `team` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `discipline` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `torch_route` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `tag` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `venue` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sports` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `end_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
